[2026-03-15T08:58:03.973Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xx41ZeUKKwKmtPz9qio3iC","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Skill Reference\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI enables you to record application sessions for performance analysis and debugging, then upload and manage those recordings.\n\n## Installation\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\nGenerate an API key from https://app.replay.io settings and store it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser and capture a session |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Submit recordings to the cloud |\n| `list` | View all local recordings |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Delete recordings locally |\n| `login/logout` | Manage account access |\n| `info` | Check CLI and browser versions |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Submit debugging symbols for a workspace |\n\n## Common Workflow\n\n1. **Record**: `replayio record https://myapp.com`\n2. **Upload**: `replayio upload <recording-id>` (if not done automatically)\n3. **Debug**: Access the recording URL to analyze performance and issues\n\n## MCP Integration\nInstall the Replay MCP Server in Claude to debug recorded applications directly using your `REPLAY_API_KEY` for authorization."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c4da05b-f48b-41c2-b979-f34be8c3cef2","uuid":"10746a64-371d-4c5e-894e-ffdd4a25fac7","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Skill Reference\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI enables you to record application sessions for performance analysis and debugging, then upload and manage those recordings.\n\n## Installation\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\nGenerate an API key from https://app.replay.io settings and store it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser and capture a session |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Submit recordings to the cloud |\n| `list` | View all local recordings |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Delete recordings locally |\n| `login/logout` | Manage account access |\n| `info` | Check CLI and browser versions |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Submit debugging symbols for a workspace |\n\n## Common Workflow\n\n1. **Record**: `replayio record https://myapp.com`\n2. **Upload**: `replayio upload <recording-id>` (if not done automatically)\n3. **Debug**: Access the recording URL to analyze performance and issues\n\n## MCP Integration\nInstall the Replay MCP Server in Claude to debug recorded applications directly using your `REPLAY_API_KEY` for authorization.","durationMs":3962,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-15T08:58:04.821Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AquVRQQA8K9GkWkFDqU7iN","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Skill File Content\n\n**Name:** replay-mcp\n\n**Description:** \"Use Replay MCP to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\"\n\n**Allowed Tools:** Bash(replayio:*), mcp__replay\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\nReplay MCP enables investigation of browser recordings by treating them as comprehensive databases of application execution. The tool captures all events during a page visit, allowing users to explore behavior with precise temporal data.\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe recommended approach involves four steps:\n1. Formulate specific questions about app behavior\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Form evidence-based conclusions\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what occurred and when:\n- Error tracking (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code inspection with execution hit counts\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events happened:\n- Stack frame inspection and control dependency analysis\n- Point descriptions with variable values\n- Expression evaluation and DOM element inspection\n- Logpoint tracking for repeated statement execution\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nA \"point\" represents a specific execution moment, while an \"element\" refers to a persistent DOM node reference independent of any particular execution point."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c4da05b-f48b-41c2-b979-f34be8c3cef2","uuid":"37fafaef-4f40-406f-86b3-f3cd474cfd12","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Skill File Content\n\n**Name:** replay-mcp\n\n**Description:** \"Use Replay MCP to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\"\n\n**Allowed Tools:** Bash(replayio:*), mcp__replay\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\nReplay MCP enables investigation of browser recordings by treating them as comprehensive databases of application execution. The tool captures all events during a page visit, allowing users to explore behavior with precise temporal data.\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe recommended approach involves four steps:\n1. Formulate specific questions about app behavior\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Form evidence-based conclusions\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what occurred and when:\n- Error tracking (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code inspection with execution hit counts\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events happened:\n- Stack frame inspection and control dependency analysis\n- Point descriptions with variable values\n- Expression evaluation and DOM element inspection\n- Logpoint tracking for repeated statement execution\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nA \"point\" represents a specific execution moment, while an \"element\" refers to a persistent DOM node reference independent of any particular execution point.","durationMs":3914,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
