searches section showing origin → destination, dates, and passenger count.\n350-\n351-### RecentSearches\n--\n373-- **Initial state**: User has performed 3 searches in order: (1) LAX→JFK, (2) SFO→ORD, (3) LAX→LHR\n374-- **Action**: User navigates back to the search page\n375-- **Expected**: All three recent searches are displayed with the most recent (LAX→LHR) shown first.\n376-\n377-#### Test: RecentSearches updates after a new search\n378:- **Components**: RecentSearches, SearchButton\n379-- **Initial state**: One recent search exists (LAX → JFK)\n380-- **Action**: User performs a new search (SFO → ORD) and returns to the search page\n381-- **Expected**: Two recent searches are displayed. The new search (SFO → ORD) appears first, followed by the older one (LAX → JFK).\n382-\n383-### PopularDestinations\n--\n393-- **Initial state**: Popular destinations section is visible\n394-- **Action**: User examines a destination card\n395-- **Expected**: The card displays the destination city name, country name, a colored gradient image placeholder, and a starting price (e.g., \"from $199\").\n396-\n397-#### Test: PopularDestinations clicking a card initiates a search\n398:- **Components**: PopularDestinations, AirportAutocomplete, SearchButton\n399-- **Initial state**: Popular destinations section is visible, user has no origin set\n400-- **Action**: User clicks on a destination card (e.g., \"Tokyo, Japan\")\n401-- **Expected**: The destination field is populated with the corresponding airport. A search is initiated to that destination (the origin may use a default or prompt the user to enter one).\n402-\n403-#### Test: PopularDestinations displays multiple cards in grid layout"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c4da05b-f48b-41c2-b979-f34be8c3cef2","uuid":"821b44e2-53b0-47c2-ae1e-6afd31533baf","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"6-- TripTypeSelector\n7-- PassengerCountSelector\n8-- CabinClassSelector\n9-- AirportAutocomplete\n